SYNTHETIC
MEASURED_SANDBOX

EXTERNAL-INSPIRATION CONTEXT
Developmental lateral inhibition is a known local symmetry-breaking mechanism:
initially similar neighboring cells can amplify small differences and adopt complementary fates.

Decentralized task-allocation systems in social insects also show:
local demand / response thresholds can generate flexible division of labor.

These are inspiration only.

H70 evidence is the synthetic experiment below.

GENERIC TRANSFORMATIONS
Each region can express one of three phenotypes:

T0
specialized compute-heavy transformation.

T1
specialized memory-heavy complementary transformation.

G
generalist local completion.

No region is assigned:
T0
or
T1.

SPECIALIST RESOURCE COSTS
T0:
[2 compute, 0.5 memory] per intermediate.

T1:
[0.5 compute, 2 memory] per completed downstream use.

A completed specialized workflow requires:
one T0 output
+
one T1 use.

GENERALIST
Local full workflow:

[5 compute, 5 memory].

This creates a real efficiency advantage for coordinated specialization.

