ROLE-EXPRESSION STATE
Each region carries one continuous local differentiation variable:

s_i in [-1,1].

positive:
express T0.

negative:
express T1.

near zero:
generalist / undifferentiated.

No global role count is visible.

LOCAL DIFFERENTIATION UPDATE
Exploratory form:

new role tendency
depends on:

1.
local log compute/memory ratio;

2.
negative coupling to neighboring role tendency;

3.
small local noise;

4.
optional slow retained causal role prior.

The neighbor-negative term is generic:

IF MY NEIGHBOR IS STRONGLY EXPRESSING ONE EXTREME,
PRESS AWAY FROM THAT SAME EXTREME.

This is the computational lateral-inhibition motif.

During link partition:
specialized expression is suppressed
and
generalist completion is used.

Stored differentiation tendency is not erased.

