PRIMARY DUAL-TIMESCALE RESULT
A weak slow prior can retain:
historical role tendency

without:
preventing fast phenotype reversal.

This is the role-specialization analogue of H6:

STORED PRIOR
!=
CURRENT EXPRESSION AUTHORITY.

PARTITION RESULT
During the communication partition:

specialized inter-region exchange is unavailable.

All viable policies fall back to:

approximately 30.32
generalist workflows/step.

The specialization state is not destroyed.

When communication returns:
the complementary phenotype re-expresses.

Thus:

ROLE CAPABILITY
CAN REMAIN STORED

while:

ROLE EXPRESSION
is temporarily suppressed.

RELATION TO H69
H69:
roles reverse when resource niches reverse,
but the two role types are externally defined.

H70:
which region occupies which role
emerges from local symmetry breaking.

The transformation repertoire remains given.

Therefore H70 advances:
ROLE ASSIGNMENT EMERGENCE

but not yet:
ROLE / TRANSFORMATION INVENTION.

RELATION TO DEVELOPMENTAL LATERAL INHIBITION
The useful computational motif is not:
copy biology literally.

It is:

LOCAL NEGATIVE FEEDBACK
CAN TURN SMALL DIFFERENCES
INTO COMPLEMENTARY SPECIALIZATION.

This may be reusable for:
- compute vs state roles;
- relay vs sensing roles;
- repair vs growth roles;
- local resource-processing niches.

RELATION TO H6 / H23 / H25
The same architecture pattern recurs:

SHARED RULE

+
FAST REVERSIBLE EXPRESSION

+
SMALL SLOW RETAINED PRIOR

rather than:
hard permanent identity.

GENERAL PRINCIPLE
Yggdrasil should distinguish:

ROLE CAPABILITY

ROLE TENDENCY / MEMORY

CURRENT ROLE EXPRESSION.

Those are three different things.

Do not collapse them into:
one permanent cell type.

DECISION
AR-H70 is POSITIVE WITH A CAUSAL-ROLE-LOCK-IN LIMIT.

Supported synthetically:

- complementary computational roles can emerge from initially symmetric regions;
- no region requires a preassigned role identity;
- lateral local differentiation breaks symmetry reliably;
- local metabolic resource ratios bias role orientation when niches exist;
- roles reverse after niche reversal;
- partition can suppress role expression without erasing capability;
- directly feeding past causal success into fast role state causes lock-in;
- weak slow role prior plus fast expression preserves reversibility.

Not demonstrated:

- discovery of new transformations;
- more than two complementary roles;
- many-cell role proportions;
- noisy/adversarial neighbor differentiation;
- role inheritance during cell division;
- real task-level functional intermediates.

NEXT HIGH-VALUE MOVE
AR-H71 — ROLE ECOLOGY / MANY-CELL PROPORTION CONTROL WITHOUT GLOBAL HISTOGRAM

Two cells make complementary differentiation easy.

A real tissue may need:

